cacert.pem is the bundle of root certificates that curl extracts from
Mozilla's NSS store (certdata.txt) and publishes at
https://curl.se/ca/cacert.pem. Mozilla distributes certdata.txt under the
Mozilla Public License 2.0 (https://www.mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/) and the
extracted bundle carries the same licence. The file's own header names the
date of the Mozilla data it was made from; tools/roots.sh refreshes it and
checks the published sha256 on the way.

The update fetch (launcher/tls.c) compiles it in as the roots a channel's
certificate must chain to. mmo/FEED.md says what that buys.
